99xj|n|The act of supplying; supplial. ; That which supplies a want; sufficiency of things for use or want. ; Auxiliary troops or reenforcements. ; The food, and the like, which meets the daily necessities of an army or other large body of men; store; -- used chiefly in the plural; as, the army was discontented for lack of supplies. ; An amount of money provided, as by Parliament or Congress, to meet the annual national expenditures; generally in the plural; as, to vote supplies. ; A person who fills a place for a time; one who supplies the place of another; a substitute; esp., a clergyman who supplies a vacant pulpit.	a:4g7z,86,47;v36,85,60;7kic,84,4;39v1,81,5;a3o6,78,5;7kjo,78,2;a3or,77,135;6s8t,76,4;a2ho,73,61;6s8s,70,5;y2j,69,308;7b8a,69,3;a4a7,68,11;v3n,68,9;774e,67,80~7b8f,33,3840;68i1,43,3375;8pm3,24,3051;7aas,35,2461;2t0u,60,2022;a800,14,1870;9ra8,26,1614;218w,7,1134;2okx,41,993;34dz,22,890;5hu9,7,884;aeh5,65,757;8mqp,15,727;59f2,25,607;43bd,17,594	v:akkh,76,9;1ivu,65,124;2pmv,65,17;6s8r,63,7;6s8s,62,3;10fr,61,11;7v3x,60,297;a3or,60,41;12ty,59,61;a2lj,57,2;77kv,56,258;6s8u,54,3;7b8a,53,1;alu9,52,16;7xf1,52,5~9bfs,31,513;7v3x,60,297;77kv,56,258;4ooo,24,149;3cqs,17,134;1ivu,65,124;7sna,3,82;5i2g,31,76;4f20,12,75;5931,20,64;12ty,59,61;ai9w,50,56;4es3,7,54;7q63,12,48;a2yo,20,47	V:28rb,77,1023;5kfi,73,6;7t21,64,12;2ns7,64,6;8864,59,11;3d3e,55,6;2pmu,53,2;q9a,52,5;8hhq,51,87;aehd,51,514;1ul7,51,4;45ri,50,41;6rw3,50,2;6e50,49,5;8nrw,47,112~28rb,77,1023;1rz5,19,825;7owb,25,653;3sf5,11,565;68ew,5,533;aehd,51,514;7q63,46,512;75b6,36,424;7i03,16,351;1olc,3,340;1ons,6,196;3a4b,24,195;37h9,39,167;7i07,14,163;7bak,47,160	n:7b8f,86,147346;mz4,82,309;2ga,80,15;9bg0,79,32;9t6g,79,26;4rdi,76,4;aa3p,75,11;1xih,69,18;5ofj,69,23;2edj,68,2;7kjo,68,1;znb,67,5;akkh,65,4;aa3k,64,10;oyd,64,9~7b8f,86,147346;agmu,51,6553;5xog,56,5216;aeh9,43,4243;27ds,60,4039;1kf,49,1680;770u,6,1417;a800,6,1070;3e5j,38,760;t32,29,686;7wk,26,656;52uh,62,540;3kq6,31,524;a6aa,16,465;72yo,25,460	N:28r9,84,